<article class="env-lemma" id="01KW">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/01KW">Lemma <span data-tag="01KW">26.21.16</span>.</a> Let $f : X \to S$ be a morphism. Assume $f$ is separated and $S$ is a separated scheme. Suppose $U \subset X$ and $V \subset X$ are affine open. Then $U \cap V$ is affine (and a closed subscheme of $U \times V$). </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      In this case $X$ is separated by Lemma <a href="/tag/01KU" data-tag="01KU">26.21.12</a>. Hence $U \cap V$ is affine by applying Lemma <a href="/tag/01KP" data-tag="01KP">26.21.7</a> to the morphism $X \to \mathop{\mathrm{Spec}}(\mathbf{Z})$. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>